<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Geldria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Geldria was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fort at Pulicat, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coromandel-coast">Coromandel Coast</a> of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, built in 1613. It was the headquarters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>'s Coromandel governorate for most of the 17th century and a base for the textile and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trades</a> with South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>. Its remains and a Dutch cemetery survive in modern Pulicat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-geldria.jpg" alt="Fort Geldria" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: McKay Savage · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:India_-_Pulicat_Lake_-_003_-_entrance_to_the_Dutch_cemetery.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
